      "message": "If you are asserting in seri at the end of a test, you may want to use `expect` instead.\n\nassert will fail and throw at the first failure, while expect will run all the check and only throw when reaching the end of the test.\n\nSo that perfect here.\n\nSee https://truth.dev/expect.html#why-you-should-use-expect\n\nNote that you don\u0027t want to use it everywhere especially in \"test setup\" for which you don\u0027t even want the test to continue processing if the preliminary assertion failed",
